{"agent":"recover-lk","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"When `[locks].mode` is `\"log\"`, the new branch returns `_HookResult(result=\"logged\", note=denial)` immediately on `CK.REFUSE`, before the existing Bash forbidden-command filter below. That filter is therefore skipped. Concrete input: `mode=\"log\"`, `p.tool=\"Bash\"`, `tool_input={\"command\": \"git stash -- /path/held-by-other.txt\"}`. `CK.paths_of` returns `/path/held-by-other.txt`, `CK.verdict` returns `CK.REFUSE` because another agent’s lease covers that file, and the hook returns `\"logged\"` (allow), so the forbidden `git stash` command runs. `log` mode is supposed to log the lease refusal and allow the write, not to disable the independent `[hooks].forbidden_commands` refusal.","digest":"2291301eea0f3fe1","family":"deepseek","location":"ddflow/api/setup/hooks.py:276-277","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/setup/hooks.py:276-277"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"The holder clause is derived only from the first rejected path: `holder = _holder(repo, agent, bad[0])`. In a multi-file write with `bad = [\"notes.txt\", \"shared.txt\"]`, where `notes.txt` is outside the lease and unheld but `shared.txt` is outside the lease and held by agent `bob`, the refusal names both files but omits `bob holds it`, because `_holder` is never called for `shared.txt`. This violates the stated requirement that a write to a held file is refused with the holder, and a single first path is not enough when one refusal covers multiple bad paths.","digest":"4fec8722d661732c","family":"deepseek","location":"ddflow/services/swarm/lanehooks_check.py:verdict","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/swarm/lanehooks_check.py:verdict"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"The new test asserts the refusal message contains `\"ddflow suggestions\"`, but the change intent and the advertised CLI next call say the send-a-suggestion option is `\"ddflow suggest\"`. A refusal produced to satisfy this test (or an implementation that already emits it) will tell a blocked agent to run a command that does not exist for that option, so one of the promised remediation calls is unusable. The direct `CK.verdict(...)` call in this test demonstrates the wrong string in `msg`.","digest":"4a83ae27742a54f9","family":"deepseek","location":"tests/test_write_hook_wire.py:32","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_write_hook_wire.py:32"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"`test_verdict_names_the_holder_and_the_options` asserts `assert \"ddflow suggestions\" in msg`, which contradicts the intent stating \"ddflow suggest\" (singular), causing a test failure when the implementation uses the subcommand `ddflow suggest` or vice-versa.","digest":"b3fac763c992aac3","family":"google","location":"tests/test_write_hook_wire.py:33","reviewer":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_write_hook_wire.py:33"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"With `[locks].mode=log`, a tool whose payload has paths and a lease `REFUSE` returns `_HookResult(result=\"logged\")` immediately. That skips the forbidden-command check that follows for Bash/`run_shell_command`/`shell`. Input: mode `log`, tool `Bash`, `paths_of` yields a path outside the live lease, and `tool_input.command` is `git push`. `verdict` refuses the path, the function returns logged, and `git push` is never denied. Enforce used to stop the tool before that check; log must still enforce forbidden commands while only allowing the out-of-lease write.","digest":"5a6e76841e30adef","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/api/setup/hooks.py:275","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/setup/hooks.py:275"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"`_holder` is called only on `bad[0]`, then the same name is attached to every refused path. Input: `bad == [\"src/a.py\", \"src/b.py\"]`, `src/a.py` matched by nobody else's lease, `src/b.py` covered by agent `other`'s live glob. The refusal is `src/a.py, src/b.py is outside the item's lease globs (...); wait ...` with no holder, so the agent that actually holds `src/b.py` is omitted. If `bad[0]` is held by `X` and `bad[1]` by `Y`, the text says `X` holds both.","digest":"809964e693a39a16","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/swarm/lanehooks_check.py:137","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/swarm/lanehooks_check.py:137"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"`test_verdict_names_the_holder_and_the_options` requires the substring `ddflow suggestions`. The contract this change claims to enforce (D-lock-lifecycle-answers, and the stated options `ddflow wait`, `ddflow suggest`, `ddflow task add` in CLI and MCP form) is `ddflow suggest`. A refusal that names that exact next call fails the test; a message that passes names a different command and is never required to include the MCP form, so the wire check locks in the wrong option.","digest":"8c56e5688054695c","family":"xai","location":"tests/test_write_hook_wire.py:33","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_write_hook_wire.py:33"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":12904,"diff_sha":"cc0c85a77a1e4a0a6942f14d3c744d776521a481b3a66eb7b5b1495ee1d952a5","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":1.2,"excluded_bytes":2615,"excluded_files":1,"excluded_paths":["README.md"],"family":"deepseek","findings":7,"max_chunk_chars":12000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","output_digest":"8faad58f355ab575","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/LK-write-hook-wire.rubber_duck.gemini-3.5-flash-lite.20261107T223817Z-82d9a3b6.jsonl","reason":"","review_degraded":[{"at":1794090709.5274017,"family":"moonshot","gate":"rubber_duck","model":"kimi-for-coding-highspeed","reason":"HTTP 429","reviewer":"kimi-k3"}],"review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2],"reviewed_head":"76885b7debd2be05d775e2f411504cb5aed58bc2","reviewed_paths":{"README.md":"100644 fe6db45d0972fff80f7326ab9554856bf9955394","ddflow/api/setup/hooks.py":"100644 28e22cb26ebd437ba0b33fc873b9b6d1ec5108af","ddflow/config_sections/locks.py":"100644 4f536f49c90898761e24d083f926d05072d92cfc","ddflow/services/claudehooks.py":"100644 b47972a24dde0a4098cef33512913631de8806f1","ddflow/services/hookwriters/__init__.py":"100644 adcea02bd76b5656c21452a7f8ea9169996fe1a1","ddflow/services/swarm/lanehooks_check.py":"100644 8965cf9c2cc5cbcc6748728529d3bb7c9cf8170b","ddflow/templates/upgrade/unreleased/knob_added.locks.mode.toml":"100644 8973784761495a38e6fc270ec64433699a0f78f5","tests/test_hook_table.py":"100644 cb78b7c6c7f807653aca1d8cd2f79e261cf9f3e4","tests/test_write_hook_wire.py":"100644 ab486f8e81cc8169115243cc2bd022dc3dc348e2"},"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","reviewer_digest":"dd08c1466c2b8632","reviewer_families":["deepseek","google","xai"],"round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/api/setup/hooks.py:276-277","ddflow/services/swarm/lanehooks_check.py:verdict","tests/test_write_hook_wire.py:32","tests/test_write_hook_wire.py:33","ddflow/api/setup/hooks.py:275","ddflow/services/swarm/lanehooks_check.py:137","tests/test_write_hook_wire.py:33"],"tree_sha":"76885b7debd2+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"7 finding(s)"},"id":"e67f6bf60ea628918346c7f7f","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":150841,"schema":1,"subject":"LK-write-hook-wire","ts":"2026-11-07T22:39:34.108218Z"}
